# task-14 fd-scan proof — induced mid-negotiation throw, /proc/self/fd accounting
# harness: /tmp/opencode/t14-harness/fdscan.cpp
#   PHASE A = 3x Swapchain ctor against a gate-OFF backend with a DIFFERENT
#             game device uuid -> openContext hard-errors inside
#             validateExchangeDescriptors AFTER all exchange fds were exported,
#             duplicated and the timeline syncFd created (the flagged window).
#   PHASE B = control: successful same-device context open+close roundtrip x2.
# scenario geometry: multiplier=2 -> 2 source + 1 dest exchange fds.
#
# fd ledger for PHASE A per attempt:
#   layer creates: 3 exchange originals + 3 desc dups + syncFd original
#                  (+1 syncFd dup in fixed builds only)
#   prefix (HEAD): syncFd original + 3 desc dups leak  => steady +4/attempt
#   fixed  (t14):  syncFd original janitor-closed; cross-device hands the
#                  ORIGINAL to openContext (backend provably never consumes
#                  it); only the 3 desc dups leak (documented T13 residual)
#                                                     => steady +3/attempt

===== PREFIX (git HEAD a4af910, pre-fix) =====
PHASE_A baseline=6
PHASE_A attempt=1 fds=12 delta=6      # +2 one-time error-path init, then +4
PHASE_A attempt=2 fds=16 delta=10     # +4/attempt steady-state leak
PHASE_A attempt=3 fds=20 delta=14     # +4/attempt steady-state leak
PHASE_B baseline=21
PHASE_B r1 alive fds=22 delta=1
PHASE_B r1 closed fds=22 delta=1      # +1 one-time process residual (see below)
PHASE_B r2 alive fds=19 delta=1       # (rerun with 2 rounds)
PHASE_B r2 closed fds=19 delta=1      # NOT per-context: one-time only

===== FIXED (t14 worktree) =====
PHASE_A baseline=6
PHASE_A attempt=1 fds=11 delta=5      # +2 one-time error-path init, then +3
PHASE_A attempt=2 fds=14 delta=8      # +3/attempt steady-state (desc dups only)
PHASE_A attempt=3 fds=17 delta=11     # +3/attempt steady-state (desc dups only)
PHASE_B baseline=18
PHASE_B r1 alive fds=19 delta=1
PHASE_B r1 closed fds=19 delta=1
PHASE_B r2 alive fds=19 delta=1       # one-time residual confirmed non-growing
PHASE_B r2 closed fds=19 delta=1

# VERDICT
# - flagged syncFd window: FIXED. prefix leaked the syncFd ORIGINAL on every
#   openContext pre-import failure (+4/attempt); fixed leaks zero sync fds
#   (+3/attempt, -1 per attempt vs prefix, exactly the flagged fd).
# - remaining +3/attempt = handed descriptor DUPLICATES on early openContext
#   failure: documented-pre-existing T13 residual (frozen backend contract
#   leaves unconsumed descriptor fds caller-owned; closing them from the layer
#   risks double-closing driver-consumed fd numbers). Bounded: multiplier+1
#   once per failed context creation.
# - PHASE_B success path returns to baseline modulo a ONE-TIME +1 process
#   residual present IDENTICALLY in prefix and fixed builds (first-success
#   driver/iostream allocation; round 2 proves it does not grow per context).
